A plain Debian cloud disk, written by hand from the mkosi documentation.

Upstream: https://github.com/systemd/mkosi/blob/v27.1/mkosi/resources/man/mkosi.1.md (the
          settings and the repart definitions of a bootable disk), not a tree mkosi ships.
License:  LGPL-2.1-or-later (the documentation it follows); this tree is tundravm's.
Files:    mkosi.conf and mkosi.repart/ (an ESP and an ext4 root).
Exercises: Mirror= and Snapshot=, Format=disk with Bootable=yes, a bootloader and UKI
          choice, KernelCommandLine= with the console the image owns, KernelModules= with a
          glob, Locale=, Timezone=, Hostname=, WithDocs=, WithRecommends=, RootPassword=,
          Ssh=, Checksum=, RepartDirectories= and the VM sizing of [Runtime].
